  "code": "2847",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><br>ANA-LIA MAXX is an indirect membrane based enzyme immunoassay of IgG class antibodies.</p>\n<p><strong>CLINICAL SIGNIFICANCE</strong><br>4) SmD1: Antibodies to Sm have a high specificity (~95%) for Disseminated Lupus Erythematosus. Together with antibodies to dsDNA, they<br>can be considered path gnomonic for this condition, but occur in only 5 - 10% of patients. On the other hand, the SmD1 synthetic peptide of<br>Sm has been shown to significantly improve sensitivity (Upto 70%) without affecting the specificity. This is an ACR criterion marker for SLE.<br>Ref: Contrad et al. Autoantibodies in systemic autoimmune diseases - A diagnostic reference Published by Pabst Science Publishers 2007.</p>\n<p><strong>LIMITATIONS</strong>:<br>* A positive result must be used in association with clinical evaluation and diagnostic procedure.<br>* Samples from apparent blood donor may contain autoantibodies.<br>* If the sample contains elevated levels of immune complexes or other immunoglobulin aggregates, false positive result cannot be ruled<br>out.</p>",
